# Binding requirements (do not shorten)

This is the last pass. Do not stop at a partial port. Do not treat this file as a 7-bullet substitute for the keep-list.

1. **100% official OpenCode features** on the single live path. Never weaker than official at any layer. Never dropped.
2. **100% of features introduced after the session change** stay on that path: PromptTape, memory, loop-control, sandbox, exec-policy, hooks, worktree, plan-gate, and every other added capability. Only stronger than official.
3. **One path only.** HTTP/TUI/CLI: Session prompt → SessionRunner → core ToolRegistry → `packages/core/src/tool/*`.
4. **Parallel implementation files must be deleted from disk** after their behavior is on the live path. Unregistering or “not constructing” is not deletion. Features must survive the delete.
5. Loop is already live, independently usable, on by default. Abort must not be cleared by the next drain. Do not restore `runLoop`. Do not wrap drain in `Effect.uninterruptible`. Do not add a second loop.
6. Do not add or leave leftover files/exports named v1/v2 that the user can see. Historical SQL migrations with v2 in the name stay. Do not half-rename SessionV2.
7. No TODOs left for a later round.
8. Keep-list in `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-07-v1-runtime-inventory.md` and Hard freeze in `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-15-capability-gap-roadmap.md` must stay provable on the live path.
9. Out of scope (reference comparison, not official regressions): Codex/Hermes/Grok product modules (toolsets, codebase-graph, Pi session trees, marketplaces, IM/gateway, Starlark, Guardian, computer-use).
10. Tests from package dirs only. Do not weaken live tests. Do not touch `~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json`.
